<script>
  import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.pulse';
  import Footer from '../../components/Footer.pulse';

  let title = "Pulse v0.16.0 Released";
  let subtitle = "The Correctness & Speed Update: adopt-and-bind hydration, unified compiler, keyed List with LIS, createSelector, and a hardened runtime.";
  let date = "September 24, 2026";
</script>

<Navbar />

<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <div class="header">
      <span class="date">{date}</span>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">{subtitle}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        We are excited to announce <strong>Pulse v0.16.0</strong> — a release focused on
        <strong>correctness and measured speed</strong>. Hydration now adopts the SSR DOM instead of remounting,
        the SFC compiler is unified, keyed lists reconcile with a prefix/suffix + Map strategy, and several
        security-sensitive paths were hardened. This post describes only changes that landed in PRs #1–#6.
      </p>

      <h2>💧 Adopt-and-bind hydration</h2>
      <p>
        The client finds the SSR root (<code>data-p-h</code> or the first child), passes <code>_hydrationNode</code>,
        and <strong>does not</strong> call <code>replaceWith</code> when the tree matches. List and Show run in
        <strong>host mode</strong>: the host stays in place while keyed rows (<code>data-p-key</code>) and branches
        are adopted and effects are attached. Markers also include <code>data-p-list</code> and <code>data-p-show</code>.
        On mismatch or a missing root, Pulse falls back to a client render with <code>onMismatch</code> and a
        dev <code>console.warn</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Local measurement (HeadlessChrome via <code>bench/</code>, SSR HTML already in the document):</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>hydrate_1k</strong> keyed rows: ~0.2 ms median</li>
          <li><strong>remount_1k</strong> keyed rows: ~1.0 ms median</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin:0">Adopt is ~5× faster than remount for this case (no node allocation). These are
        <strong>local measurements</strong> — not js-framework-benchmark scores. See <code>bench/RESULTS.md</code>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>🧩 Unified SFC compiler</h2>
      <p>
        Interactive compilation goes through a single shared path at <code>src/compiler</code> (server
        <code>ComponentCompiler</code>); the bundler interactive path delegates to it. Bare leading script-less
        SFCs are peeled correctly before HTML parse. Emit remains <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> + <code>cloneNode</code>
        + path/effect bindings (SFC-native). Local benches showed <code>createElement</code> slightly faster on a
        tiny row shape; that tradeoff is documented and may be revisited later.
      </p>

      <h2>🧬 Reactive state &amp; text bindings</h2>
      <p>
        The state façade now exposes <strong>getters and setters</strong>, so <code>state.count++</code> and
        assignments work. Text bindings wrap values with <code>String(...)</code> and update inside effects.
        Expression evaluation goes through <code>safeEvalExpr</code> instead of ad-hoc per-evaluation
        <code>new Function</code> call sites.
      </p>

      <h2>📋 Keyed List (prefix/suffix + Map + LIS)</h2>
      <p>
        <code>&lt;List&gt;</code> uses keyed Map reuse with a common prefix/suffix skip. For the changed middle range,
        it now computes a <strong>longest increasing subsequence</strong> and only moves rows that are not part of it,
        and it only does that when surviving rows actually moved. Swapping two rows in a 1,000-row list used to
        <code>insertBefore</code> most of the middle; now it moves only the rows that changed position. Pure appends and creates skip LIS.
        Explicit <code>key</code> is wired through the template transformer and mount. Duplicate keys print a warning
        in development (the last item with a key wins). List virtualization remains available; <strong>FLIP is opt-in</strong>
        via <code>flip: true</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Local List measurement (append_1k after 1k rows):</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>prefix/suffix + Map: ~2.6–2.7 ms</li>
          <li>always-insertBefore: ~5.4–5.9 ms</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>🎯 createSelector and createRoot</h2>
      <p>
        The core runtime now has <code>createSelector</code>, so a row asks "am I selected?" and only the rows
        whose answer changed are notified when the selection moves. Selecting a row touches two rows instead of all of
        them. <code>createRoot</code> gives each List row its own ownership scope, so removing a row disposes its effects.
      </p>

      <h2>🖱️ One listener on tbody</h2>
      <p>
        The js-framework-benchmark entry attaches a single delegated click listener to the <code>&lt;tbody&gt;</code>
        and finds the row with <code>closest("tr")</code>, instead of adding handlers to every row. Row creation
        stays a template <code>cloneNode</code> plus two small effects (label and selected class).
      </p>

      <h2>🛠️ Compiler and build fixes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>List item <code>class</code> and attribute bindings stay on the item instead of being hoisted to the page root.</li>
        <li>Class attributes written as nested template literals now emit valid JavaScript, so the docs site minifies with terser.</li>
        <li>Compiled components import <code>pulse/runtime</code> instead of hard-coded <code>/runtime/*.js</code> paths.</li>
        <li>The production runtime is no longer empty: <code>RuntimeBuilder</code> finds the moved runtime files and transpiles TypeScript before minifying, and <code>bun run build</code> writes <code>dist/runtime/*.js</code> plus <code>dist/index.d.ts</code>.</li>
        <li>The dev server now loads and serves the real <code>hydrate</code>, so SSR pages actually hydrate during development.</li>
        <li><code>tsc --noEmit</code> is clean. About 20 type errors were fixed, mostly wrong import paths, without ts-ignore.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>🔒 Security</h2>
      <p>
        The template transformer no longer calls <code>new Function</code>. It goes through a shared safe evaluator
        instead. This builds on the earlier move to <code>safeEvalExpr</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>📊 js-framework-benchmark (local run)</h2>
      <p>
        We ran the js-framework-benchmark CPU tests locally: Chrome 151, headless, 10 iterations, with vanillajs,
        Solid 1.9.3, Vue 3.5.39, and Pulse in the <strong>same run</strong>. Pulse divided by vanilla JS (median total time):
      </p>
      <div class="highlight-box">
        <ul>
          <li>Create 1,000 rows: <strong>1.11×</strong></li>
          <li>Replace all rows: 1.15×</li>
          <li>Update every 10th row: 1.19×</li>
          <li>Select a row: <strong>1.14×</strong></li>
          <li>Swap two rows: <strong>1.13×</strong></li>
          <li>Remove a row: 1.06×</li>
          <li>Create 10,000 rows: 1.17×</li>
          <li>Append 1,000 rows: 1.16×</li>
          <li>Clear all rows: 1.39×</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin:0">Geometric mean: <strong>about 1.16× vanilla JS</strong>. In the earliest local run, before
        LIS and createSelector, swap was about 6.3× vanilla and the geometric mean was about 1.39×. These are
        <strong>local measurements</strong>, not official leaderboard results. Full tables are in
        <code>benchmarks/js-framework-benchmark/RESULTS.md</code>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>🔒 Hardened error UI</h2>
      <p>
        Error-boundary and HMR error surfaces use <code>textContent</code> / DOM APIs instead of HTML injection.
        Dev-tool imports were fixed (<code>errors-v2</code> → <code>errors</code>).
      </p>

      <h2>📦 Versions &amp; project hygiene</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>pulse-framework</strong> and <strong>pulse-app</strong>: 0.16.0</li>
        <li><strong>VS Code extension</strong>: remains 1.5.0 (no code changes in this release)</li>
        <li>Added CHANGELOG, ROADMAP, CONTRIBUTING, Code of Conduct, SECURITY, issue/PR templates, and CI</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Limitations (honest)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Comment text markers (<code>&lt;!--p--&gt;</code>) exist, but text binding mostly still uses path walk; not every compiler emit path is fully marker-driven yet.</li>
        <li>Deep HTML mismatch falls back rather than surgical patch.</li>
        <li>Clearing all rows is still the weakest benchmark case (about 1.39× vanilla JS).</li>
        <li>The benchmark entry uses the runtime API directly, not a compiled <code>.pulse</code> file.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Full details live in <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> and the PR descriptions for #1–#6. Next up: finish
        comment-marker hydration across emit paths, keep sizing the runtime honestly, and make clearing rows faster.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />

